## 7. Honest Residual (5 of 27 suites fail)

The runner is deterministic. The 5 failing suites are real test failures in the underlying assertions, not runner defects. The failing suites likely check current state of the repository (e.g., specific files in specific locations, specific text in specific headers) that has drifted since the tests were authored. Fixing each failing assertion is a separate task and out of scope for this runner-level audit.

The 5 failures are visible in the double-run output and the user can investigate them individually. The runner's job is to be a deterministic surface for running them; the assertions are the responsibility of the underlying test authors.

